          "cover_letter": "I'm an administrative professional who believes organized support makes every team more effective. Over the last 1.5 years at MedFirst Clinic, I've managed calendars for 3 physicians across 2 locations while coordinating 15+ meetings weekly and maintaining HIPAA-compliant records. There are two things that make me a great fit for this position.\n\nFirst, I'm experienced at managing multiple executive calendars simultaneously. At MedFirst, I coordinated schedules for 3 physicians across 2 clinic locations, booking 15+ meetings weekly in Outlook while handling last-minute changes and conflicts. This multi-executive scheduling experience maps directly to supporting Northwind Health's leadership team. Second, I have hands-on experience organizing confidential records in a healthcare setting. I maintained patient and staff documentation under strict HIPAA compliance at MedFirst Clinic, ensuring records were accurate, accessible, and secure. That is exactly the kind of confidential document management this role requires.\n\nNorthwind Health's focus on patient-centered care aligns with my belief that good admin work directly supports better health outcomes. I'm also excited about Northwind's expansion into telehealth. Supporting a team through that kind of growth is the challenge I'm looking for. I think you'll find my experience is a strong fit for Northwind Health, and I'd welcome the chance to discuss it further."
        }
